---
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<section class="section section--sunken" id="who" aria-labelledby="who-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section__head">
      <h2 class="display-2" id="who-title">Who it's for</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="audience">
      <div class="audience__lead reveal">
        <span class="who__lead-icon"><Icon name="wifi" /></span>
        <h3 class="title-lg">WiFi users</h3>
        <p class="lead">
          No more worrying about whether a network is legit or whether an attacker might be tricking you.
          If a network claims a registered name and doesn't match, you see it before you type anything.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="audience__list">
        <li class="audience__item reveal" style="--reveal-index: 1">
          <Icon name="building" />
          <h3 class="title">Network operators</h3>
          <p class="caption">Companies, universities and other organizations. Register once and stop attackers from stealing internal credentials.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="audience__item reveal" style="--reveal-index: 2">
          <Icon name="landmark" />
          <h3 class="title">Federations and standards bodies</h3>
          <p class="caption">eduroam, the Wireless Broadband Alliance: password protection that doesn't rely on every user configuring their device correctly.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="audience__item reveal" style="--reveal-index: 2">
          <Icon name="phone" />
          <h3 class="title">Device and operating system vendors</h3>
          <p class="caption">Improve platform security and trust, while reducing the burden on users to configure their devices correctly.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .who__lead-icon { color: var(--color-accent-default); }
  .who__lead-icon :global(.icon) { width: var(--space-8); height: var(--space-8); }
</style>
